The fix/deep-dive-4 batch on trn1.2xlarge, 2026-09-13 (tree e542ac79, i.e. through
d59f00f): the measured window on every row, memory_write's DMA and engine counters,
the true NEFF candidate total, and allocation_fragmentation's device read-back.

What each change shows here:

  - elapsed_s on every row. memory_read reads 20.07 s of loop beside a
    Duration of 314.72 s -- the gap the field exists to expose.
  - memory_write's side of "which side set the rate": dma_active 0.883,
    vector_engine_active 0.0000226. The write path is DMA-bound; the producer
    is essentially idle. (memory_read: dma 0.938, consumer engine 0.650.)
    Recorded, not interpreted in code.
  - profiler_candidates_available 3 and 4, matching the NEFFs actually present
    in each kernel's directory (listed at the end). Both are under the
    16-candidate budget, so the above-budget case -- where the old count capped
    at 16 against 63 present -- is not exercised by this run; the unit tests
    cover it. What this shows is that an in-budget count is unchanged.
  - allocation_fragmentation: retained_element 1.0 across 832 surviving blocks;
    the allocations reached the device, and the row passes at 2418.8 events/s.
  - Scores unchanged: 543.68 / 536.57 / 273.04 / 274.44 GB/s against
    543.78 / 537.39 / 272.90 / 274.08 on 2026-09-12.

Found by this run: the aggregates' elapsed_s was the whole worker phase
(577.4 s on memory_read_agg beside a 20 s loop), not the window the Score
divides by -- fixed in the commit this log accompanies.

